# MantaTrimmer.py and pico/main.py were authored on Windows and are stored with
# CRLF. Take git out of the line-ending business entirely: store the bytes as
# they are, on every platform, so nothing silently rewrites them.
#
# This matters because a tool that flips the endings turns a 400-line review into
# a 5000-line whole-file diff, which is how this branch nearly shipped. If you
# edit these files with a script, write bytes, not text.
*.py -text
*.md -text
*.json -text
*.txt -text
*.csv -text
